<ul style="margin: 20px 0 20px 24px; line-height: 2.2;">
  <li><strong>Acquisition Zone:</strong> Properties within the proposed right-of-way shown in the Volume 2 mapbook would be acquired once the project is funded. UDOT's earlier stated standard was 250 feet wide (125 feet on each side of the centerline); the draft maps show the actual proposed footprint, including interchanges and frontage roads.{% cite "udot-draft-ses-vol2-nov2026" %}</li>
  <li><strong>Noise Evaluation Zone (500 feet):</strong> Properties within ~500 feet of the highway centerline are evaluated for noise impacts (66 dBA threshold). Some may qualify for sound wall mitigation.</li>
  <li><strong>Construction Impact Zone:</strong> Properties near the corridor may experience temporary construction traffic, dust, vibration, and noise during the construction phase.</li>
  <li><strong>Indirect Impact Zone:</strong> Properties along feeder roads and at the 4000 South interchange may experience increased traffic after construction.</li>
</ul>

<div class="callout">
  <p><strong>To find your property's location:</strong></p>
  <ol>
    <li>Visit <a href="https://www.webercountyutah.gov/assessor/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Weber County Assessor's Office (webercountyutah.gov/assessor)</a></li>
    <li>Search for your address or parcel number in their online mapping tool</li>
    <li>Note the parcel number (format: TR-##-[##]-[###]-###)</li>
    <li>Register for State Environmental Study updates at <a href="https://udotinput.utah.gov/sr177extension" rel="noopener noreferrer">udotinput.utah.gov/sr177extension</a> to receive study updates; the Draft State Environmental Study and its maps are on the Materials &amp; Documents tab</li>
  </ol>
</div>

