<div class="section-label jump-target" id="decision-points">Step 4: Timeline & Decision Points</div>
<h2>When Do You Need to Act?</h2>

<table>
  <caption>Critical timeline for Phase 3 property owners</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Date / Milestone</th>
      <th scope="col">What Happens</th>
      <th scope="col">Your Action</th>
      <th scope="col">Why It Matters</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Nov 6, 2026 (done)</strong></td>
      <td>Draft State Environmental Study published, identifying a Preferred Alternative; Volume 2 maps the proposed right-of-way</td>
      <td>Find your parcel in the Volume 2 mapbooks; note relocation, partial acquisition, access, or noise-wall impacts</td>
      <td><strong>FIRST FORMAL PUBLIC MAPS</strong> for determining whether you're affected</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Now – Dec 11, 2026</strong></td>
      <td>Formal comment period; in-person public hearing Nov 10 at Roy Junior High School, with right-of-way specialists available</td>
      <td>Submit written comments if affected (email, online form, mail, or at the hearing)</td>
      <td>Last chance to influence the alignment before the Final State Environmental Study</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Early 2027 (expected)</strong></td>
      <td>Final State Environmental Study published with responses to comments, then approved</td>
      <td>Check whether your parcel's impacts changed; UDOT may make voluntary Corridor Preservation offers</td>
      <td>Alignment becomes official once approved; negotiations may start</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>2027–2029</strong></td>
      <td>Design phase (if funded) / Corridor Preservation ongoing</td>
